1
00:01:31,164 --> 00:01:32,197
<v PETER> Hello?

2
00:01:32,207 --> 00:01:34,788
<v JAN> Oh hello. My name's Jan.

3
00:01:34,798 --> 00:01:39,986
<v JAN> Are you the right person to talk to about the Buckworth Conservation Group?

4
00:01:39,996 --> 00:01:42,402
<v PETER> Yes, I'm Peter. I'm the secretary.

5
00:01:42,412 --> 00:01:48,214
<v JAN> Good. I've just moved to this area, and I'm interested in getting involved.

6
00:01:48,224 --> 00:01:51,095
<v JAN> I was in a similar group where I used to live.

7
00:01:51,105 --> 00:01:54,725
<v JAN> Could you tell me something about your activities, please?

8
00:01:54,735 --> 00:01:59,883
<v PETER> Of course. Well, we have a mixture of regular activities and special events.

9
00:01:59,893 --> 00:02:03,974
<v PETER> One of the regular ones is trying to keep the beach free of litter.

10
00:02:03,984 --> 00:02:09,304
<v PETER> A few of us spend a couple of hours a month on it, and it's awful how much there is to clear.

11
00:02:09,314 --> 00:02:12,951
<v PETER> I wish people would be more responsible and take it home with them.

12
00:02:12,961 --> 00:02:14,530
<v JAN> I totally agree.

13
00:02:14,540 --> 00:02:17,030
<v JAN> I'd be happy to help with that.

14
00:02:17,040 --> 00:02:19,227
<v JAN> Is it OK to take dogs?

15
00:02:19,237 --> 00:02:22,514
<v PETER> I'm afraid not, as they're banned from the beach itself.

16
00:02:22,524 --> 00:02:26,454
<v PETER> You can take them along the cliffs, though. And children are welcome.

17
00:02:26,464 --> 00:02:27,544
<v JAN> Right.

18
00:02:27,554 --> 00:02:32,134
<v PETER> We also manage a nature reserve, and there's a lot to do there all year round.

19
00:02:32,144 --> 00:02:40,852
<v PETER> For example, because it's a popular place to visit, we spend a lot of time looking after the paths and making sure they're in good condition for walking.

20
00:02:40,862 --> 00:02:43,309
<v JAN> I could certainly help with that.

21
00:02:43,319 --> 00:02:47,670
<v PETER> Good. And we have a programme of creating new habitats there.

22
00:02:47,680 --> 00:02:59,360
<v PETER> We've just finished making and installing nesting boxes for birds to use, and next we're going to work on encouraging insects - they're important for the biodiversity of the reserve.

23
00:02:59,370 --> 00:03:00,740
<v JAN> They certainly are.

24
00:03:00,750 --> 00:03:07,539
<v PETER> Oh, and we're also running a project to identify the different species of butterflies that visit the reserve.

25
00:03:07,549 --> 00:03:10,056
<v PETER> You might be interested in taking part in that.

26
00:03:10,066 --> 00:03:17,398
<v JAN> Sure. I was involved in something similar where I used to live, counting all the species of moths.

27
00:03:17,408 --> 00:03:18,639
<v JAN> I'd enjoy that.

28
00:03:18,649 --> 00:03:26,228
<v PETER> Another job we're doing at the reserve is replacing the wall on the southern side, between the parking area and our woodshed.

29
00:03:26,238 --> 00:03:29,329
<v PETER> It was badly damaged in a storm last month.

30
00:03:29,339 --> 00:03:30,009
<v JAN> ОK.

31
00:04:10,806 --> 00:04:17,052
<v PETER> Then as I said, we have a programme of events as well, both at the weekend, and during the week.

32
00:04:17,062 --> 00:04:21,378
<v JAN> Right. I presume you have guided walks?

33
00:04:21,388 --> 00:04:25,968
<v JAN> I'd like to get to know the local countryside, as I'm new to the area.

34
00:04:25,978 --> 00:04:26,946
<v PETER> Yes, we do.

35
00:04:26,956 --> 00:04:30,836
<v PETER> The next walk is to Ruston Island, a week on Saturday.

36
00:04:30,846 --> 00:04:39,576
<v PETER> We'll be meeting in the car park at Dunsmore Beach at low tide - that's when the sands are dry enough for us to walk to the island without getting wet.

37
00:04:39,586 --> 00:04:40,857
<v JAN> Sounds good.

38
00:04:40,867 --> 00:04:43,587
<v PETER> The island's a great place to explore.

39
00:04:43,597 --> 00:04:46,868
<v PETER> It's quite small, and it's got a range of habitats.

40
00:04:46,878 --> 00:04:52,677
<v PETER> It's also an ideal location for seeing seals just off the coast, or even on the beach.

41
00:04:52,687 --> 00:04:59,095
<v JAN> OK. And is there anything we should bring, like a picnic, for instance?

42
00:04:59,105 --> 00:05:02,405
<v PETER> Yes, do bring one, as it's a full-day walk.

43
00:05:02,415 --> 00:05:08,655
<v PETER> And of course it'll be wet walking across and back, so make sure your boots are waterproof.

44
00:05:08,665 --> 00:05:13,164
<v JAN> I must buy a new pair - there's a hole in one of my current ones!

45
00:05:13,174 --> 00:05:16,933
<v JAN> Well, I'd definitely like to come on the walk.

46
00:05:16,943 --> 00:05:23,251
<v PETER> Great. Then later this month we're having a one-day woodwork session in Hopton Wood.

47
00:05:23,261 --> 00:05:25,351
<v JAN> I've never tried that before.

48
00:05:25,361 --> 00:05:28,409
<v JAN> Is it OK for beginners to take part?

49
00:05:28,419 --> 00:05:36,896
<v PETER> Definitely. There'll be a couple of experts leading the session, and we keep the number of participants down, so you'll get as much help as you need.

50
00:05:36,906 --> 00:05:40,537
<v JAN> Excellent! I'd love to be able to make chairs.

51
00:05:40,547 --> 00:05:43,435
<v PETER> That's probably too ambitious for one day!

52
00:05:43,445 --> 00:05:49,055
<v PETER> You'll be starting with wooden spoons, and of course learning how to use the tools.

53
00:05:49,065 --> 00:05:52,368
<v PETER> And anything you make is yours to take home with you.

54
00:05:52,378 --> 00:05:55,678
<v JAN> That sounds like fun. When is it?

55
00:05:55,688 --> 00:05:59,216
<v PETER> It's on the 17th, from 10 a.m. until 3.

56
00:05:59,226 --> 00:06:07,127
<v PETER> There's a charge of £35, including lunch, or £40 if you want to camp in the wood.

57
00:06:07,137 --> 00:06:09,859
<v JAN> I should think I'll come home the same day.

58
00:06:09,869 --> 00:06:13,131
<v JAN> Well, I'd certainly like to join the group.